2026-10-11T07:09:24.5547677Z To enable CUDA support, UCX requires the CUDA Runtime library (libcudart).
2026-10-11T07:09:24.5548114Z The library can be installed with the appropriate command below:
2026-10-11T07:09:24.5548347Z 
2026-10-11T07:09:24.5548495Z * For CUDA 12, run:    conda install cuda-cudart cuda-version=12
2026-10-11T07:09:24.5548852Z * For CUDA 13, run:    conda install cuda-cudart cuda-version=13
2026-10-11T07:09:24.5549057Z 
2026-10-11T07:09:24.5549241Z If any of the packages you requested use CUDA then CUDA should already
2026-10-11T07:09:24.5549570Z have been installed for you.
2026-10-11T07:09:24.5549710Z 
2026-10-11T07:09:24.5549713Z 
2026-10-11T07:09:24.5549867Z To enable CUDA support, please follow UCX's instruction above.
2026-10-11T07:09:24.5550103Z 
2026-10-11T07:09:24.5550259Z To additionally enable NCCL support, run:    conda install nccl
2026-10-11T07:09:24.5550483Z 
2026-10-11T07:09:24.5550491Z 
2026-10-11T07:09:24.5550674Z On Linux, Open MPI is built with CUDA awareness but it is disabled by default.
2026-10-11T07:09:24.5551040Z To enable it, please set the environment variable
2026-10-11T07:09:24.5551325Z OMPI_MCA_opal_cuda_support=true
2026-10-11T07:09:24.5551711Z before launching your MPI processes.
2026-10-11T07:09:24.5552024Z Equivalently, you can set the MCA parameter in the command line:
2026-10-11T07:09:24.5552353Z mpiexec --mca opal_cuda_support 1 ...
2026-10-11T07:09:24.5552695Z Note that you might also need to set UCX_MEMTYPE_CACHE=n for CUDA awareness via
2026-10-11T07:09:24.5553098Z UCX. Please consult UCX documentation for further details.
